## Summary

Implemented **`DET.CTA.HIERARCHY`** as a deterministic DOM check: at most **one primary CTA** per logical viewport region (hero, open modal/panel, sticky footer).

### Source rule → signals

From `docs/design/ux-audit/deterministic-design-rules.md#det-cta-hierarchy`:

- **Pass:** one primary CTA per hero / sticky footer / modal band  
- **Evidence:** button-class scan (`btn-primary`, `btn-forge`; excludes outline/secondary/link)

### Files changed

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-cta-hierarchy.check.js` | Full implementation: `collectCtaHierarchyReport`, `findingsFromCtaHierarchyReport`, `run` |
| `design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js` | Registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS` as **implemented** (`conversion`, `trustAndEcosystemTruth`, `major`, weight **9**) |
| `design-rules/registry.generated.json` | `DET.CTA.HIERARCHY` → **implemented**; coverage **15** implemented / **35** stub |
| `auditor-tests/det-cta-hierarchy.test.js` | Unit tests for report → findings and `run` |

### Check behavior

- **Regions:** KS hero shells (`.landing-hero*`, `.product-hero`), visible modals (`.modal.show`, `.offcanvas.show`, `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal`), sticky/fixed bottom bands  
- **Primary detection:** same pattern as `DET.CARD.ACTION_LIMIT` (`btn-primary`, `btn-forge`; not outline/secondary)  
- **Findings:** `severity` major/critical, `area: conversion`, standard `message` / `evidence` / `remediation`  
- **Runtime:** uses `metrics.ctaHierarchyReport` or live `page` via Playwright (same pattern as button-group / card-action checks)

Legacy `cta-trust-ecosystem` check still maps to this rule ID; the new rule adds **primary-per-region** enforcement separate from “too many CTAs above fold.”

### Verification (please run locally)

Shell was not available in this session. From `tools/website-ux-auditor`:

```bash
npm run blend-rules
npm test
```

`blend-rules` will refresh `registry.generated.json` **fingerprint** (manual registry edits may differ slightly until then). `npm test` includes `auditor-tests/det-cta-hierarchy.test.js` and re-runs the blender smoke test.
